From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opi5 <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: rk3588s-orangepi-5-pro: let PCIe switch
 vcc3v3_phy1

The YT6801's supply is regulator-always-on and regulator-boot-on, so
pcie_dw_rockchip's remove hook can't switch it off before the OS:
regulator_set_enable() refuses for always-on, and with boot-on the
regulator is enabled twice (autoset, then the PCIe driver), so one
disable leaves it on.

Drop both in U-Boot's DT. The PCIe driver switches the supply on
itself before training the link, and Linux's DT is unchanged.
rk3588-u-boot.dtsi is what the build included before, by SoC.
---
 arch/arm/dts/rk3588s-orangepi-5-pro-u-boot.dtsi | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/dts/rk3588s-orangepi-5-pro-u-boot.dtsi

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3588s-orangepi-5-pro-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3588s-orangepi-5-pro-u-boot.dtsi
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7e298b7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3588s-orangepi-5-pro-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0+ OR MIT)
+
+#include "rk3588-u-boot.dtsi"
+
+/*
+ * Let the PCIe driver own the YT6801's supply: it switches it on in
+ * rockchip_pcie_init_port() and off again before the OS starts. With
+ * regulator-always-on U-Boot can't switch it off, and with regulator-boot-on
+ * the extra enable keeps it on (enable_count 2).
+ */
+&vcc3v3_phy1 {
+	/delete-property/ regulator-always-on;
+	/delete-property/ regulator-boot-on;
+};
